IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, s 105: recovery of benefit payments. Layer 1, part wra4.
-- Section 105 inserts ss 71ZB to 71ZH into the Social Security Administration Act 1992 (SSAA) and makes conforming
-- changes. The inserted sections are what the person meets: what may be recovered from them, from whom, and how.
-- Host Acts named in labels: SSAA, SSA1998 (Social Security Act 1998), JSA (Jobseekers Act 1995). They are not among the
-- sources: what they say elsewhere is a borrowed fact, asked as an input.
-- Seams taken as inputs (PLAN.md section 8): seam 2 and 3 (universal credit: the s 8(1) amount and the s 3 entitlement),
-- seam 4 (s 28(2)(f)), seam 5 (JSA 19C(2)(f)), seam 6 (the host-Act recoverability of the 71ZH(1)(c) to (e) payments).
-- Result convention: JUST FALSE / FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not covered (see wra4-ss96-97.l4).

§ `s 105 SSAA 71ZB -- recovery of overpayments of certain benefits`

-- 71ZB(1): "paid in excess of entitlement" is the part of what was paid that exceeds what the person was entitled to.
-- src:1678 | (1) The Secretary of State may recover any amount of the following paid in excess of entitlement—
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) (src:1678-1678)
GIVEN `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount the person was entitled to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the amount paid in excess of entitlement` MEANS
    IF `the amount paid` GREATER THAN `the amount the person was entitled to`
    THEN `the amount paid` MINUS `the amount the person was entitled to`
    ELSE 0

-- 71ZB(1)(a), universal credit: the entitlement is the s 8(1) amount where the claimant was entitled (s 3), otherwise nil.
-- src:1679 | (a) universal credit,
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1)(a) (src:1679-1679)
GIVEN `s 3 the claimant is entitled to universal credit for the period` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Were you entitled to universal credit for the period?
      `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` IS A NUMBER  @desc What was the amount of universal credit you were entitled to for the period, in pounds?
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER  @desc How much universal credit was paid to you for the period, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1)(a) the universal credit paid in excess of entitlement` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the amount paid in excess of entitlement` `the amount paid`
        (IF `s 3 the claimant is entitled to universal credit for the period` THEN `s 8(1) the amount of the award of universal credit for the period` ELSE 0)

-- 71ZB(1): the Secretary of State "may recover" an overpayment of (a) universal credit, (b) jobseeker's allowance, (c)
-- employment and support allowance and (d) "except in prescribed circumstances" housing credit. A benefit the list does
-- not name is outside the grant (not a "no": the grant is limited by its own wording).
-- src:1678 | (1) The Secretary of State may recover any amount of the following paid in excess of entitlement—
-- src:1679 | (a) universal credit,
-- src:1680 | (b) jobseeker's allowance,
-- src:1681 | (c) employment and support allowance, and
-- src:1682 | (d) except in prescribed circumstances, housing credit (within the meaning of the State Pension Credit Act 2002).
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) (src:1678-1682)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
      `prescribed circumstances apply to the housing credit` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc If the benefit is housing credit: do the prescribed circumstances apply that stop an overpayment of it being recovered? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the Secretary of State may recover an overpayment of the benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `universal credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `contributory employment and support allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `housing credit` THEN
        CONSIDER `prescribed circumstances apply to the housing credit`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE                    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except in prescribed circumstances, housing credit" (the circumstances apply)
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the circumstances are prescribed
    WHEN `income support` THEN NOTHING                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `housing benefit` THEN NOTHING                   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `council tax benefit` THEN NOTHING               -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `child tax credit` THEN NOTHING                  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `working tax credit` THEN NOTHING                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `state pension credit` THEN NOTHING              -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `personal independence payment` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `disability living allowance` THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `industrial injuries benefit` THEN NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `social fund payment` THEN NOTHING               -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `child benefit` THEN NOTHING                     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `guardian's allowance` THEN NOTHING              -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `bereavement allowance` THEN NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `incapacity benefit` THEN NOTHING                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `maternity allowance` THEN NOTHING               -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `severe disablement allowance` THEN NOTHING      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `widow's pension` THEN NOTHING                   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `widowed mother's allowance` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"
    WHEN `widowed parent's allowance` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the grant is "any amount of the following"

-- A plain membership test used by 71ZB(6): is the benefit one the subsection (1) list names? (Not a legal answer.)
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) (src:1678-1682)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the benefit is named in the list` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `universal credit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `contributory employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `income-related employment and support allowance` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `housing credit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE                                       -- a membership test, not a legal "no": the benefit is not named in subsection (1)

-- 71ZB(2): recoverable from the person to whom it was paid, or such other person as may be prescribed.
-- src:1683 | (2) An amount recoverable under this section is recoverable from—
-- src:1684 | (a) the person to whom it was paid, or
-- src:1685 | (b) such other person (in addition to or instead of the person to whom it was paid) as may be prescribed.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) (src:1683-1685)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom the amount was paid` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the amount paid to you?
      `regulations prescribe the person as one from whom it is recoverable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations prescribe you as another person from whom the amount is recoverable? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person to whom the amount was paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE (CONSIDER `regulations prescribe the person as one from whom it is recoverable`
          WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "(a) the person to whom it was paid, or (b) such other person ... as may be prescribed"; the text does not say that nobody else is liable
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)                      -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such other person ... as may be prescribed"

-- 71ZB(3): an amount paid under a determination "is not recoverable ... unless" the determination was reversed or varied on
-- appeal, or revised or superseded, "except where regulations otherwise provide". This answers whether the bar applies.
-- src:1686 | (3) An amount paid in pursuance of a determination is not recoverable under this section unless the determination has been—
-- src:1687 | (a) reversed or varied on an appeal, or
-- src:1688 | (b) revised or superseded under section 9 or section 10 of the Social Security Act 1998,
-- src:1689 | except where regulations otherwise provide.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) (src:1686-1689)
GIVEN `the amount was paid in pursuance of a determination` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the amount paid because of a decision (a "determination") about your entitlement?
      `the determination has been reversed or varied on an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has that decision been reversed or varied on an appeal?
      `the determination has been revised or superseded under section 9 or 10 of the Social Security Act 1998` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has that decision been revised or superseded (SSA 1998 ss 9 and 10)?
      `regulations otherwise provide` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations provide that the amount is recoverable even though the decision has not been reversed, varied, revised or superseded? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(3) the determination does not bar recovery` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the amount was paid in pursuance of a determination`))
        THEN NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of amounts "paid in pursuance of a determination"
        IF `the determination has been reversed or varied on an appeal` OR `the determination has been revised or superseded under section 9 or 10 of the Social Security Act 1998`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE (CONSIDER `regulations otherwise provide`
                   WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                   WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not recoverable under this section unless the determination has been" reversed, varied, revised or superseded
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "except where regulations otherwise provide"

-- 71ZB(5): universal credit paid for the sole reason that prescribed income was paid after its prescribed date is treated
-- as paid in excess of entitlement.
-- src:1691 | (5) Where an amount of universal credit is paid for the sole reason that a payment by way of prescribed income is made after the date which is the prescribed date for payment of that income, that amount is for the purposes of this section paid in excess of entitlement.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(5) (src:1691-1691)
GIVEN `the amount is of universal credit` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the amount universal credit?
      `it was paid for the sole reason that prescribed income was paid after the prescribed date for paying it` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the amount paid only because income of yours (a kind regulations prescribe) reached you after the date it was due?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(5) the amount is treated as paid in excess of entitlement` MEANS
    IF `the amount is of universal credit` AND `it was paid for the sole reason that prescribed income was paid after the prescribed date for paying it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the deeming applies "for the sole reason" stated; any other case is for 71ZB(1)

-- 71ZB(6): an amount paid to one of persons awarded a benefit jointly may be regarded as paid to the other.
-- src:1692 | (6) In the case of a benefit referred to in subsection (1) which is awarded to persons jointly, an amount paid to one of those persons may for the purposes of this section be regarded as paid to the other.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(6) (src:1692-1692)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
      `the benefit is awarded to persons jointly` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the benefit awarded to you and another person jointly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(6) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` MEANS
    IF `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(1) the benefit is named in the list` `the benefit` AND `the benefit is awarded to persons jointly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "a benefit referred to in subsection (1) which is awarded to persons jointly"

-- 71ZB(7): "without prejudice to any other means of recovery", an amount may be recovered by (a) deduction from benefit,
-- (b) deduction from earnings, (c) the courts, (d) adjustment of benefit.
-- src:1693 | (7) An amount recoverable under this section may (without prejudice to any other means of recovery) be recovered—
-- src:1694 | (a) by deduction from benefit (section 71ZC);
-- src:1695 | (b) by deduction from earnings (section 71ZD);
-- src:1696 | (c) through the courts etc (section 71ZE);
-- src:1697 | (d) by adjustment of benefit (section 71ZF).
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) (src:1693-1697)
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of recovering an amount`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) an amount recoverable under 71ZB may be recovered in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `deduction from benefit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `deduction from earnings` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `court action` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adjustment of benefit` THEN TRUE

§ `s 105 SSAA 71ZC -- deduction from benefit`

-- 71ZC(1): by deducting the amount from payments of "prescribed benefit".
-- src:1699 | (1) An amount recoverable from a person under section 71ZB may be recovered by deducting the amount from payments of prescribed benefit.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZC(1) (src:1699-1699)
GIVEN `the benefit payment is of a benefit regulations prescribe for deductions` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Is the payment one of the benefits that regulations prescribe for recovering an overpayment by deduction? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZC(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from this payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit payment is of a benefit regulations prescribe for deductions`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the power is "payments of prescribed benefit"; the text does not say a deduction is barred from others
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed benefit"

-- 71ZC(2): an amount paid to the person on behalf of another may be recovered from the person by deduction from (a)
-- prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled, (b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed to the
-- person by the person on whose behalf it was paid, (c) the same where the obligation is owed by any other person.
DECLARE `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) source of the deduction` IS ONE OF
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled`
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid`
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(c) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by any other person`

-- src:1700 | (2) Where an amount recoverable from a person under section 71ZB was paid to the person on behalf of another, subsection (1) authorises its recovery from the person by deduction—
-- src:1701 | (a) from prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled,
-- src:1702 | (b) from prescribed benefits paid to the person to discharge (in whole or in part) an obligation owed to that person by the person on whose behalf the recoverable amount was paid, or
-- src:1703 | (c) from prescribed benefits paid to the person to discharge (in whole or in part) an obligation owed to that person by any other person.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) (src:1700-1703)
GIVEN `the amount was paid to the person on behalf of another` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the amount paid to you on behalf of someone else?
      `the source of the deduction` IS A `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) source of the deduction`
      `the benefits are prescribed benefits` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Are the benefits the ones regulations prescribe for deductions? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) the amount paid on behalf of another may be recovered by deduction from this source` MEANS
    IF `the amount was paid to the person on behalf of another`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the benefits are prescribed benefits`
          WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): each source is "prescribed benefits"
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)                      -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed benefits"
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): subsection (2) applies "where an amount ... was paid to the person on behalf of another"

-- 71ZC(3): a (2)(b) obligation "shall in prescribed circumstances be taken to be discharged by the amount of the deduction".
-- src:1704 | (3) Where an amount is recovered as mentioned in paragraph (b) of subsection (2), the obligation specified in that paragraph shall in prescribed circumstances be taken to be discharged by the amount of the deduction.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) (src:1704-1704)
GIVEN `the source of the deduction` IS A `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) source of the deduction`
      `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Are the circumstances ones that regulations prescribe for treating the obligation as discharged? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZC(3) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source of the deduction`
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` THEN
        CONSIDER `the circumstances are prescribed circumstances`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): discharge "in prescribed circumstances"; the text does not say it is not discharged otherwise
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                         -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "prescribed circumstances"
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): subsection (3) is about paragraph (b)
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(c) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by any other person` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): subsection (3) is about paragraph (b)

-- 71ZC(4): a (2)(c) obligation "shall in all cases be taken to be so discharged".
-- src:1705 | (4) Where an amount is recovered as mentioned in paragraph (c) of subsection (2), the obligation specified in that paragraph shall in all cases be taken to be so discharged.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZC(4) (src:1705-1705)
GIVEN `the source of the deduction` IS A `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2) source of the deduction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZC(4) the obligation is taken to be discharged by the deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the source of the deduction`
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(c) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by any other person` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(a) prescribed benefits to which the person is entitled` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): subsection (4) is about paragraph (c)
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZC(2)(b) prescribed benefits paid to discharge an obligation owed by the person on whose behalf the amount was paid` THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): subsection (4) is about paragraph (c)

§ `s 105 SSAA 71ZD -- deduction from earnings`

-- 71ZD(1): regulations may provide for amounts recoverable under 71ZB to be recovered by deductions from earnings.
-- src:1707 | (1) Regulations may provide for amounts recoverable under section 71ZB to be recovered by deductions from earnings.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) (src:1707-1707)
GIVEN `regulations provide for deductions from earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations provide for overpayments to be recovered by deductions from earnings? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZD(1) the amount may be recovered by deduction from earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `regulations provide for deductions from earnings`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                          -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Regulations may provide"; the text does not say no deduction otherwise
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulations are not among the sources

-- 71ZD(2): "earnings" has such meaning as may be prescribed.
-- src:1708 | (2) In this section “earnings” has such meaning as may be prescribed.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) “earnings” (src:1708-1708)
GIVEN `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do the regulations treat this payment as earnings for these deductions? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZD(2) the payment is earnings` MEANS
    `regulations prescribe the payment as earnings`       -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "has such meaning as may be prescribed"; the answer is the regulations' own, when supplied

-- 71ZD(3)(a): regulations may require the person from whom an amount is recoverable to disclose details of their employer.
-- src:1710 | (a) requiring the person from whom an amount is recoverable (“the beneficiary”) to disclose details of their employer, and any change of employer, to the Secretary of State;
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(a) (src:1710-1710)
GIVEN `the amount is recoverable from the person under section 71ZB` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is an overpayment recoverable from you?
      `the regulations include provision requiring disclosure of employer details` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do the regulations require you to tell the Secretary of State who your employer is, and of any change? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(a) the person may be required to disclose details of their employer` MEANS
    IF `the amount is recoverable from the person under section 71ZB`
    THEN (CONSIDER `the regulations include provision requiring disclosure of employer details`
          WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
          WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING                    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): regulations "may include"; the text does not say that they must
          WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING)                      -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): regulations are not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "the person from whom an amount is recoverable (“the beneficiary”)"

-- 71ZD(3)(e): regulations may set "a level of earnings below which earnings must not be reduced".
-- src:1714 | (e) as to a level of earnings below which earnings must not be reduced;
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) (src:1714-1714)
GIVEN `the earnings` IS A NUMBER  @desc What are your earnings for the period, in pounds?
      `the level of earnings below which the regulations forbid reducing earnings` IS A MAYBE NUMBER  @desc What is the level of earnings, in pounds, below which the regulations say your earnings must not be reduced? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 105 SSAA 71ZD(3)(e) the most that may be deducted from the earnings` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the level of earnings below which the regulations forbid reducing earnings`
    WHEN JUST level THEN
        IF `the earnings` GREATER THAN level
        THEN JUST (`the earnings` MINUS level)
        ELSE JUST 0                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "earnings must not be reduced" below the level (nothing may be deducted)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                             -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the level is set by regulations

§ `s 105 SSAA 71ZE -- court action`

-- 71ZE(1), (2): the amount is recoverable through the county court (England and Wales) "if the county court so orders", and
-- may be enforced in Scotland as if under an extract registered decree arbitral. For anywhere else the section is silent.
-- src:1724 | (1) Where an amount is recoverable under section 71ZB from a person residing in England and Wales, the amount is, if the county court so orders, recoverable—
-- src:1727 | (2) Where an amount is recoverable under section 71ZB from a person residing in Scotland, the amount recoverable may be enforced as if it were payable under an extract registered decree arbitral bearing a warrant for execution issued by the sheriff court of any sheriffdom in Scotland.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) (src:1724-1727)
GIVEN `where the person resides` IS A Place  @desc Where do you live?
      `the county court orders` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Has the county court ordered that the amount may be recovered through the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZE(1) and (2) the amount may be enforced through the courts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the person resides`
    WHEN `Greater London` THEN
        IF `the county court orders` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the amount is, if the county court so orders, recoverable" (no order)
    WHEN `England outside Greater London` THEN
        IF `the county court orders` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the amount is, if the county court so orders, recoverable" (no order)
    WHEN Wales THEN
        IF `the county court orders` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the amount is, if the county court so orders, recoverable" (no order)
    WHEN Scotland THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN NOTHING                  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section provides for England and Wales and for Scotland
    WHEN `outside the United Kingdom` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the section provides for England and Wales and for Scotland

-- 71ZE(3): the Secretary of State's costs of recovering under the section may be recovered as if they were amounts under 71ZB.
-- src:1728 | (3) Any costs of the Secretary of State in recovering an amount of benefit under this section may be recovered by him as if they were amounts recoverable under section 71ZB.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZE(3) (src:1728-1728)
GIVEN `the costs are the Secretary of State's costs of recovering an amount of benefit under section 71ZE` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are the costs the Secretary of State's costs of recovering the amount through the courts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZE(3) the costs of recovery may be recovered as if recoverable under 71ZB` MEANS
    IF `the costs are the Secretary of State's costs of recovering an amount of benefit under section 71ZE`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "Any costs of the Secretary of State in recovering an amount of benefit under this section"

§ `s 105 SSAA 71ZG -- recovery of payments on account`

-- src:1741 | (1) The Secretary of State may recover any amount paid under section 5(1)(r) (payments on account).
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZG(1) (src:1741-1741)
GIVEN `the payment` IS A Payment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZG(1) the Secretary of State may recover the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the payment`'s `the kind of payment`
    WHEN `a payment on account` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a payment of an award` THEN NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the power is over "any amount paid under section 5(1)(r) (payments on account)"
    WHEN `a hardship payment` THEN NOTHING                -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): a hardship payment is for 71ZH

-- src:1742 | (2) An amount recoverable under this section is recoverable from—
-- src:1743 | (a) the person to whom it was paid, or
-- src:1744 | (b) such other person (in addition to or instead of the person to whom it was paid) as may be prescribed.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZG(2) (src:1742-1744)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom the amount was paid` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the payment on account paid to you?
      `regulations prescribe the person as one from whom it is recoverable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations prescribe you as another person from whom the amount is recoverable? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZG(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` `the person is the person to whom the amount was paid` `regulations prescribe the person as one from whom it is recoverable`

-- src:1746 | (4) In the case of a payment on account of a benefit which is awarded to persons jointly, an amount paid to one of those persons may for the purposes of this section be regarded as paid to the other.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZG(4) (src:1746-1746)
GIVEN `the payment on account is of a benefit awarded to persons jointly` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the benefit awarded to you and another person jointly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZG(4) the amount paid to one of them may be regarded as paid to the other` MEANS
    IF `the payment on account is of a benefit awarded to persons jointly`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "a payment on account of a benefit which is awarded to persons jointly"

-- 71ZG(5): 71ZC, 71ZD and 71ZE apply to these amounts as to 71ZB amounts (not 71ZF, adjustment, which it does not name).
-- src:1747 | (5) Sections 71ZC, 71ZD and 71ZE apply in relation to amounts recoverable under this section as to amounts recoverable under section 71ZB.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZG(5) (src:1747-1747)
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of recovering an amount`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZG(5) the amount may be recovered in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `deduction from benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `deduction from earnings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `court action` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `adjustment of benefit` THEN NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (5) names sections 71ZC, 71ZD and 71ZE only; 71ZB(7) lists adjustment for amounts under 71ZB

§ `s 105 SSAA 71ZH -- recovery of hardship payments etc`

-- 71ZH(1): the Secretary of State may recover (a) a section 28 hardship payment "which is recoverable under that section",
-- (b) a JSA 19C hardship payment likewise, (c) a JSA payment under para 8 or 8A of Schedule 1 payable at a prescribed rate under
-- para 9 and recoverable under it, (d) a JSA payment under para 10 recoverable under it, (e) a payment recoverable under the
-- Social Security Fraud Act 2001 sections listed. Whether each is recoverable under its own provision is a borrowed fact
-- (seams 4, 5, 6): an input.
DECLARE `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1) kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(a) a universal credit hardship payment under section 28`
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(b) a jobseeker's allowance hardship payment under section 19C`
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(c) a jobseeker's allowance payment under paragraph 8 or 8A of Schedule 1`
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(d) a jobseeker's allowance payment under paragraph 10 of Schedule 1`
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(e) a payment recoverable under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001`

-- src:1749 | (1) The Secretary of State may recover any amount paid by way of—
-- src:1750 | (a) a payment under section 28 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (universal credit hardship payments) which is recoverable under that section,
-- src:1751 | (b) a payment under section 19C of the Jobseekers Act 1995 (jobseeker's allowance hardship payments) which is recoverable under that section,
-- src:1752 | (c) a payment of a jobseeker's allowance under paragraph 8 or 8A of Schedule 1 to that Act (exemptions), where the allowance is payable at a prescribed rate under paragraph 9 of that Schedule and is recoverable under that paragraph,
-- src:1753 | (d) a payment of a jobseeker's allowance under paragraph 10 of that Schedule (claims yet to be determined etc) which is recoverable under that paragraph, or
-- src:1754 | (e) a payment which is recoverable under section 6B(5A)(d) or (7)(d), 7(2A)(d) or (4)(d), 8(3)(aa), (4)(d) or 9(2A)(d) or (4)(d) of the Social Security Fraud Act 2001.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1) (src:1749-1754)
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1) kind of payment`
      `s 28(2)(f) the hardship payment is recoverable under section 28` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the universal credit hardship payment one that is recoverable under section 28 of the Act (the regulations say whether hardship payments must be repaid)?
      `s 46 JSA 19C(2)(f) the hardship payment is recoverable under section 19C` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the jobseeker's allowance hardship payment one that is recoverable under section 19C of the Jobseekers Act 1995?
      `the allowance is payable at a prescribed rate under paragraph 9` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the jobseeker's allowance paid at a rate prescribed under paragraph 9 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995?
      `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(c) the payment is recoverable under paragraph 9 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the payment recoverable under paragraph 9 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995?
      `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(d) the payment is recoverable under paragraph 10 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the payment recoverable under paragraph 10 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995?
      `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(e) the payment is recoverable under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 provisions listed` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the payment recoverable under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 provisions listed in section 71ZH(1)(e)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1) the Secretary of State may recover the payment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of payment`
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(a) a universal credit hardship payment under section 28` THEN
        IF `s 28(2)(f) the hardship payment is recoverable under section 28` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "which is recoverable under that section"
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(b) a jobseeker's allowance hardship payment under section 19C` THEN
        IF `s 46 JSA 19C(2)(f) the hardship payment is recoverable under section 19C` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "which is recoverable under that section"
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(c) a jobseeker's allowance payment under paragraph 8 or 8A of Schedule 1` THEN
        IF `the allowance is payable at a prescribed rate under paragraph 9` AND `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(c) the payment is recoverable under paragraph 9 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "where the allowance is payable at a prescribed rate under paragraph 9 ... and is recoverable under that paragraph"
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(d) a jobseeker's allowance payment under paragraph 10 of Schedule 1` THEN
        IF `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(d) the payment is recoverable under paragraph 10 of Schedule 1 to the Jobseekers Act 1995` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "which is recoverable under that paragraph"
    WHEN `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(e) a payment recoverable under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001` THEN
        IF `s 105 SSAA 71ZH(1)(e) the payment is recoverable under the Social Security Fraud Act 2001 provisions listed` THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING                                      -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "a payment which is recoverable under" the listed sections

-- src:1755 | (2) An amount recoverable under this section is recoverable from—
-- src:1756 | (a) the person to whom it was paid, or
-- src:1757 | (b) such other person (in addition to or instead of the person to whom it was paid) as may be prescribed.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZH(2) (src:1755-1757)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom the amount was paid` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the payment paid to you?
      `regulations prescribe the person as one from whom it is recoverable` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN  @desc Do regulations prescribe you as another person from whom the amount is recoverable? Leave out if not known.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZH(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(2) the amount is recoverable from the person` `the person is the person to whom the amount was paid` `regulations prescribe the person as one from whom it is recoverable`

-- 71ZH(4): where universal credit or a jobseeker's allowance is claimed by persons jointly, an amount paid to one claimant
-- may be regarded as paid to the other.
-- src:1759 | (4) Where universal credit or a jobseeker's allowance is claimed by persons jointly, an amount paid to one claimant may for the purposes of this section be regarded as paid to the other.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZH(4) (src:1759-1759)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit
      `the benefit is claimed by persons jointly` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the benefit claimed by you and another person jointly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZH(4) the amount paid to one claimant may be regarded as paid to the other` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `universal credit` THEN (IF `the benefit is claimed by persons jointly` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "claimed by persons jointly"
    WHEN `contribution-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN (IF `the benefit is claimed by persons jointly` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "claimed by persons jointly"
    WHEN `income-based jobseeker's allowance` THEN (IF `the benefit is claimed by persons jointly` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): "claimed by persons jointly"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING                                     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection names universal credit and jobseeker's allowance

-- 71ZH(5): 71ZC to 71ZF apply to these amounts as to 71ZB amounts: all four ways.
-- src:1760 | (5) Sections 71ZC to 71ZF apply in relation to amounts recoverable under this section as to amounts recoverable under section 71ZB.
@ref s 105 SSAA 71ZH(5) (src:1760-1760)
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of recovering an amount`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 105 SSAA 71ZH(5) the amount may be recovered in this way` MEANS
    `s 105 SSAA 71ZB(7) an amount recoverable under 71ZB may be recovered in this way` `the way`

§ `s 105(4), (7): the penalty agreement (SSAA 115B) and the right of appeal (SSA1998 Sch 3)`

-- Substituted SSAA 115B(4): if the recipient of a notice agrees, in the specified manner, to pay the penalty, the amount is
-- recoverable from the recipient and "no criminal proceedings shall be instituted against the recipient in respect of the
-- conduct to which the notice relates".
-- src:1765 | (4) If the recipient of a notice under subsection (3) above agrees, in the specified manner, to pay the penalty—
-- src:1766 | (a) the amount of the penalty shall be recoverable from the recipient by the Secretary of State or authority; and
-- src:1767 | (b) no criminal proceedings shall be instituted against the recipient in respect of the conduct to which the notice relates.
@ref s 105(4) SSAA 115B(4) (src:1765-1767)
GIVEN `the recipient has agreed, in the specified manner, to pay the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Have you agreed, in the manner the notice specified, to pay the penalty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4) SSAA 115B(4)(b) criminal proceedings may be instituted against the recipient for the conduct` MEANS
    IF `the recipient has agreed, in the specified manner, to pay the penalty`
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no criminal proceedings shall be instituted against the recipient in respect of the conduct to which the notice relates"
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the bar applies "If the recipient ... agrees"

@ref s 105(4) SSAA 115B(4)(a) (src:1766-1766)
GIVEN `the recipient has agreed, in the specified manner, to pay the penalty` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Have you agreed, in the manner the notice specified, to pay the penalty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4) SSAA 115B(4)(a) the penalty is recoverable from the recipient` MEANS
    IF `the recipient has agreed, in the specified manner, to pay the penalty`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the penalty is recoverable "if the recipient ... agrees"

-- 115B(4A): sections 71ZC, 71ZD and 71ZE apply to the penalty as to 71ZB amounts (not 71ZF).
-- src:1768 | (4A) Sections 71ZC, 71ZD and 71ZE above apply in relation to amounts recoverable under subsection (4)(a) above as to amounts recoverable by the Secretary of State under section 71ZB above (and, where the notice is given by an authority administering housing benefit or council tax benefit, those sections so apply as if references to the Secretary of State were to that authority).
@ref s 105(4) SSAA 115B(4A) (src:1768-1768)
GIVEN `the way` IS A `Way of recovering an amount`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(4) SSAA 115B(4A) the penalty may be recovered in this way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the way`
    WHEN `deduction from benefit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `deduction from earnings` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `court action` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `adjustment of benefit` THEN NOTHING             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): 115B(4A) names sections 71ZC, 71ZD and 71ZE only

-- SSA1998 Sch 3 paras 6A and 6B (Schedule 3 is headed "decisions against which an appeal lies").
-- src:1776 | (7) In Schedule 3 to that Act (decisions against which an appeal lies), after paragraph 6 there is inserted—
-- src:1777 | 6A
-- src:1778 | A decision as to whether payment of housing credit (within the meaning of the State Pension Credit Act 2002) is recoverable under section 71ZB of the Administration Act.
@ref s 105(7) SSA1998 Sch 3 para 6A (src:1776-1778)
GIVEN `the decision is whether payment of housing credit is recoverable under section 71ZB` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the decision about whether a payment of housing credit (the housing element of state pension credit) is recoverable from you under section 71ZB of the Administration Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(7) SSA1998 Sch 3 para 6A an appeal lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is whether payment of housing credit is recoverable under section 71ZB`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): para 6A names a decision "as to whether payment of housing credit ... is recoverable under section 71ZB"

-- src:1776 | (7) In Schedule 3 to that Act (decisions against which an appeal lies), after paragraph 6 there is inserted—
-- src:1779 | 6B
-- src:1780 | A decision as to the amount of payment recoverable under section 71ZB, 71ZG or 71ZH of the Administration Act.
@ref s 105(7) SSA1998 Sch 3 para 6B (src:1776-1780)
GIVEN `the decision is as to the amount of payment recoverable under section 71ZB, 71ZG or 71ZH` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the decision about how much you must repay under section 71ZB, 71ZG or 71ZH of the Administration Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 105(7) SSA1998 Sch 3 para 6B an appeal lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is as to the amount of payment recoverable under section 71ZB, 71ZG or 71ZH`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): para 6B names a decision "as to the amount of payment recoverable under section 71ZB, 71ZG or 71ZH"
